* INCLUSION CRITERIA

Individuals with a biochemical or genetic diagnosis of methylmalonic acidemia or cobalamin disorders of any sex or ethnicity, and over 1 month of age are eligible to enroll in this protocol as well as those with suspected genetic but unknown type of MMA. Family members of affected subjects and healthy volunteers 18+ are also eligible for a subset of procedures.

Individuals with methylmalonic acidemia or cobalamin disorders of any age, sex, and ethnicity, undergoing a transplantation surgery at UPMC Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh, are eligible to participate in the tissue collection arm of the study.

EXCLUSION CRITERIA

An affected participant who meets any of the following criteria may be excluded from participation in this study at the NIH Clinical Center:

1. medically unstable;
2. residing in a hospital;
3. sub-optimal metabolic control or for any concerns arising after review of the laboratory and clinical data;
4. any patient who requires dialysis once or more/week and weighs \<40 kg;
5. any patient who is being treated for an intercurrent infection with antibiotics or has evidence of an acute infection and has metabolic symptoms;
6. any patient who does not have a regular/local metabolic, genetic or endocrine physician and/or a family physician, pediatrician, or internist;
7. any patient who may be metabolically unstable but not acutely ill;
8. and any patient or family who may not be able to institute recommendations for appropriate testing and care before visiting the NIH.

Each family may be contacted by the NIH team prior to a pending admission to confirm that the patient is metabolically stable and ready to visit the NIH in a state of relative health, with an adequate supply of special formulas, medications, supplements, and if needed, medical equipment such as feeding pumps and replacement parts for feeding tubes.

Healthy Volunteers will be excluded if they are pregnant, are being treated with antibiotics, have kidney or liver disease, are on a special diet (such as a high protein diet or taking protein supplements), or are diagnosed with severe claustrophobia or other anxiety disorders.
